WEBVTT

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:09.270
I can't take any more...!

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:13.600
--Let's go.
--Yeah.

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:17.970
Stop making such weird noises!

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.770
You're so stiff, Mizoguchi.

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:24.020
But I have a flexible mind and soul.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.600
Those are just as rigid.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.220
I'm tight with my wallet
and morals, though.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.270
What do you mean "morals"?!

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.720
Oh!

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:35.890
Kazu, what's up?

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:38.390
Koji Tono
I'm interested in joining the Men's Cheerleading Club

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.270
Oh!

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:42.390
Now we have number four!

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:51.560
Come oooooon!

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:15.470
<i>I'll put an end to spending</i>
<i>my days so thoughtlessly</i>

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:19.520
<i>I'm dying to break free of this</i>

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:25.220
<i>Since I can never take that first step forward,</i>

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:29.310
<i>you always take my hand and pull me along</i>

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:35.140
<i>You've brought me to see</i>
<i>something completely new</i>

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:37.430
<i>My whole world is changing</i>

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.640
<i>With that first step</i>

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:43.810
<i>I felt transformed</i>

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:48.810
<i>I can go anywhere; it'll work</i>
<i>out so long as we're together</i>

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:50.390
<i>Go on, fly high, </i>

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:52.020
<i>just as you are</i>

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:55.180
<i>At times you'll feel lost and scared,</i>

00:01:55.180 --> 00:02:01.680
<i>but there are so many things you</i>
<i>won't know if you never give them a go</i>

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.310
<i>Go on, fly high, </i>

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:08.180
<i>stretch out your hands until</i>
<i>you're almost touching the sky</i>

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:11.430
<i>We're not alone anymore</i>

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:16.560
<i>Together we'll fly into a new world</i>

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:39.360
<i>Ni shi xuesheng ma</i>?
[Are you a student?]

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:48.440
Right. Well, of course, you add <i>ma </i>to the end
of most interrogative sentences like so, ya see?

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:50.440
So what about our fourth guy?

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:50.440
And in Japanese, you add <i>ka</i>

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.280
to <i>desu </i>at the end of a sentence

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:54.530
to make <i>desu ka </i>for the same effect, don'cha?

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:54.610
He promised
to meet us
at the caf.

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:57.940
to make <i>desu ka </i>for the same effect, don'cha?

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:54.690
He promised
to meet us
at the caf.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:54.770
He promised
to meet us
at the caf.

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:54.860
He promised
to meet us
at the caf.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:54.940
He promised
to meet us
at the caf.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:55.020
He promised
to meet us
at the caf.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:55.110
He promised
to meet us
at the caf.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:55.190
He promised
to meet us
at the caf.

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:56.440
He promised
to meet us
at the caf.

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:59.900
What the frick!

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:01.900
What's all the commotion?

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:05.480
A bug...

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:07.940
A bug landed on me!

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:14.730
There.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.320
Thanks a lot, man!

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.230
I've never been to a place like this.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:28.400
Seriously?

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.820
Every student at Meishiin's
come here at least once.

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:34.110
My family runs a traditional
high-class restaurant.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:37.190
They've told me to avoid
cheap places like this.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:38.150
Give me a break...

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.360
Hey, man!

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.280
What's keeping my fried pork curry?

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:43.730
Ah! Coming right up!

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:46.110
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:47.440
You're going to eat that?

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:48.360
Really?

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:50.070
Cheer me on, girls!

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:52.480
And, start!

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:54.980
All right, down the hatch!

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:00.650
What in the world?

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:03.530
If you finish that in 20
minutes, it's on the house.

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:05.980
He can't possibly be our new recruit...

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:07.690
Not likely.

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:09.530
But this name...

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:12.400
I'm sure I've seen it somewhere before.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:17.190
Long time no see!

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.820
It's been a while.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:21.820
Nobody's broken your record yet.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:24.730
Koji Tono!

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:27.940
The guy with the fastest time
for the fried pork curry challenge!

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:31.360
And I totally thought it was
our old judo captain!

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:35.940
How embarrassing. That
photo's from high school...

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:37.570
Are you with the
Men's Cheerleading Club?

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:38.940
Uh, yeah.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:40.820
I'm Kazuma Hashimoto.

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:43.280
This is Haruki Bandou.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:45.570
We're both first-year sociology students.

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:49.150
Wataru Mizoguchi. First-year
business school student.

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:51.860
I'm a first-year in literature.

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:54.070
Um, can I ask you something?

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:56.070
Sure, fire away!

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:58.280
No, I'll order first...

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:01.030
One fried pork curry with
noodles and rice, please.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:02.530
Right-o!

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:05.940
Oh, that's something from the secret menu.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.900
I blew it!

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:12.320
Welp, that sucked but--

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:13.860
They ditched me!

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:16.690
What the hell, man? Why'd they run off?

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:18.480
You're 1,400 yen short.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:20.650
You're kiddin' me!

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:22.320
Thank you, come again!

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:26.730
So you texted me after seeing the flier.

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:27.780
Yeah.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:29.030
So, Ton...

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:30.070
Ton?

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:32.360
Ton, as in short for Tono.

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:33.980
What else would I be referring to?

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:35.730
Don't just call him whatever you want.

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:40.230
Well, you two are always calling
each other "Haru" and "Kazu."

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:42.610
If you like, you can call me Mizo.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:44.280
--Not happening.
--Nuh-uh.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:47.480
So, Ton, how much do you weigh?

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:48.360
Uhh--

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:50.730
Why's that the first thing you ask him?

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:53.820
Uh, about 220 pounds, I think?

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:56.150
Have you ever played a sport?

00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:57.610
No...

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:59.030
I'm sorry.

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:01.190
Hey, no need to apologize.

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:05.070
Cheerleading has positions
suited for every body type.

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:06.320
But...

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:08.320
Why cheerleading?

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:12.570
I want to change...

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:15.610
I get it.

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:22.190
"Today is the first day
of the rest of your life."

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:26.690
You mean there's no time
like the present?

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:31.400
Dixit Lester Burnham in
the movie <i>American Beauty</i>.

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:33.110
That's a great line.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:48.400
So, you said earlier that there's
a role in cheerleading for everyone?

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:50.230
Yeah, I'll explain.

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:56.440
The person holding their hands up
in the air is called the "flyer."

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:59.820
They're like the eye-catching
star of the show.

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:02.860
They do lots of jumps n' stuff,
so they need to be small and light.

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:04.150
So in our case...

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:05.730
...I'd say that's me and Haru.

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:07.150
Me?!

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:09.690
The people supporting the flyer
are called the "bases."

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:13.650
They carry the flyer on their shoulders,
steady them with their palms, and so on.

00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:15.860
It's a position suited for
someone more well-built.

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:17.150
Like Ton.

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:21.440
The person in the back
is called the "spotter."

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:25.400
They assist the bases.
Sort of like a tripod leg.

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:29.230
The spotter dictates when
to lift up the flyer and such.

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:31.230
Think of them as the control tower.

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:33.940
That's me to a T.

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:36.570
I made you all copies for reference.

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:40.110
But we still don't have
enough members, right?

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:46.030
We'll need 16 people to enter tournaments,
but our initial goal is to get 7.

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:47.360
Once we do,

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:50.650
I want us to make our debut at
the school festival in October!

00:07:55.480 --> 00:08:00.730
Bandou Gym

00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:13.440
Haru!

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:19.030
Sis...

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:24.570
Welcome back.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:29.530
I'm home.

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:32.480
Is it true you're quitting the Judo Club?

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:35.940
Well, is it?

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:37.480
Yeah.

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:39.480
Because of your injury?

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:40.690
No.

00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:42.530
Because you weren't seeing any results?

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:47.980
I'm against this, Haru.

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:50.650
Don't give up.

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:52.780
Please don't quit judo!

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:02.230
I'm sorry.

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:05.860
Whether you get results depends on
how much effort you put into it!

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:09.110
There's...

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:10.900
...something I want to...

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:13.530
Never mind.

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:31.900
Let's see...

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:35.030
The flyer, the bases,
and the spotter, was it?

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:36.650
So that means...

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:38.610
...I'm the flyer.

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:44.900
I have to do that?

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:46.940
Toda Park

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:55.480
Now you guys try it!

00:09:55.480 --> 00:09:57.230
Yes, I've got this!

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:58.150
I can do it!

00:09:58.150 --> 00:09:59.440
Here I go!

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:07.230
You're up next, Ton.

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:08.980
Uh, right!

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:13.730
What are you doing?

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:16.360
A headstand!

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:18.690
You gotta learn to do a handstand.

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:20.190
Your turn, Haru!

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:25.280
You're walking!

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:27.820
It's easier to stay balanced that way.

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:28.730
Haru.

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:29.900
Can you stop?

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:37.230
Handstands build up your muscles
and improve your sense of balance.

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:39.980
So do them daily every chance you get!

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:43.030
You should be stretching every day, too.

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:47.030
If you're not flexible, you risk injury,
and it also affects your tumbling.

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:48.820
Your... what?

00:10:48.820 --> 00:10:50.320
Tumbling.

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:52.690
Like backflips and somersaults.

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:59.110
Since you're a flyer, you need to practice
jumps and flips on a trampoline, ASAP.

00:10:59.110 --> 00:11:03.320
A-About that, I don't
think being a flyer is--

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:05.440
You'll be fine. It's doable.

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:08.190
I'm going to work hard on
my handstand. And stretching!

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:09.570
Me, too.

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:15.780
So how 'bout we do some call
and response practice next?

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:19.070
When cheering, you need
charm, enthusiasm...

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:20.230
...and a nice smile!

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:21.610
Yeah!

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:24.480
Right, everyone line up.

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:26.110
Repeat after me!

00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:27.530
Begin!

00:11:27.530 --> 00:11:29.280
Go! Fight! Win!

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:31.400
Go! Fight! Win!

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:32.940
Smile more!

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:35.320
I can't hear you, Haru!

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:36.900
Go! Fight! Win!

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:39.190
Go! Fight! Win!

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:41.440
C'mon, Haru, big smile!

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:48.690
You feeling okay?

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:49.610
Huh?

00:11:49.610 --> 00:11:51.900
I mean... with the club.

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:53.940
Oh, yeah.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:56.070
It's fun, but...

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:59.070
I wonder if I'll ever learn
to pull off a handstand.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:02.570
I've never done a sport or anything...

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:04.440
You'll be fine.

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:09.030
I mean, I hate being
the center of attention...

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:13.610
But since Kazu asked me to do it,
I decided to give it a try anyway.

00:12:13.610 --> 00:12:15.860
But, Ton...

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:19.980
You took the initiative because you
want to change yourself, right?

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:22.110
I think that's awesome.

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:24.030
So...

00:12:24.030 --> 00:12:26.440
Let's do our best.

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:27.940
Thanks.

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:31.530
Oh!

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:32.650
Tambourining!

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:34.570
You mean tumbling.

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:41.280
Hey, it's that guy.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:44.440
--The one who lost the fried pork curry challenge.
--What, you can do a backflip? Cool!

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:46.070
--Is he in the Tennis Club?
--What, you can do a backflip? Cool!

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:47.940
I can do it, too!

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:50.610
The ladybug guy.

00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:55.030
Wow!

00:12:55.030 --> 00:12:57.400
But that's got nothing to do with tennis.

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:58.480
Exactly!

00:12:58.480 --> 00:13:00.480
And neither do you.

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:05.780
Kazu?

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:07.150
Hey!

00:13:07.150 --> 00:13:08.940
We're gonna go grab some grub!

00:13:08.940 --> 00:13:10.190
--Okay!
--Okay!

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:11.280
Okay!

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:30.400
All right, cheers!

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:32.820
Cheers!

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:43.570
Wow!

00:13:43.570 --> 00:13:46.570
So you guys said you
jumped ship from another club?

00:13:46.570 --> 00:13:48.150
--Wha...?
--Ah, right!

00:13:48.150 --> 00:13:48.900
Huh?

00:13:48.900 --> 00:13:51.150
Haru, just roll with it.

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:53.570
We'll blend in this way.

00:13:53.570 --> 00:13:55.900
I dunno, you guys seem
pretty lame to me.

00:13:55.900 --> 00:14:00.230
Just 'cuz you're joining our group
doesn't mean you'll get any chicks.

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:04.650
Hey, next time let's hit that
Italian place near campus, okay?

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:06.400
Bah...

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:07.820
Italian!

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.900
You've been drinking!

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:12.070
I'm old enough to drink.

00:14:12.070 --> 00:14:13.820
Wait, you're a first-year at 20?

00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:18.820
I failed my entrance exams!
But I won't fail you!

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:21.650
You're making zero sense.

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:23.360
You guys are a riot!

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:25.900
You've got your comedy routine down!

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:27.940
Are you jokers from the Kansai region?

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:29.690
Nope! We're Tokyo-ites.

00:14:29.690 --> 00:14:30.980
Said no one from Kansai ever!

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:36.570
By the way, the name's
Soichiro. Ichiro for short.

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:37.940
And this is Gen.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:40.730
We're both super sexy
first-year business students!

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:43.530
"Both"? Since when?

00:14:43.530 --> 00:14:45.400
No, you're not supposed to laugh yet!

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:47.650
Those were some great
backflips you did earlier.

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:49.400
Ever played a sport?

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:50.820
I've always played baseball.

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:53.730
I did soccer.

00:14:53.730 --> 00:14:56.530
Yeesh, you're completely wasted.

00:14:56.530 --> 00:14:59.190
I'm not wasting any of it.

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:03.860
So you did baseball and soccer.
Then why join the Tennis Club?

00:15:03.860 --> 00:15:07.940
Well, we've always been big on sports,
but it was nuthin' but guys.

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:11.820
So we decided to join a club
with a bit more style in college.

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:14.230
How can you have style
with hair like that?

00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:16.360
But...

00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:19.150
It's not what you expected, right?

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:25.690
Come join us.

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:26.480
Huh?

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:28.400
Join your what?

00:15:30.940 --> 00:15:32.780
The Men's Cheerleading Club?

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:35.280
Aren't you here because
you bailed on another club?

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:36.860
Sorry, we lied.

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:40.570
We're here because we want to recruit you.

00:15:40.570 --> 00:15:42.230
Let's do this together!

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:45.230
Hey now...

00:15:45.230 --> 00:15:48.150
The hell are you losers up to?

00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:50.980
Huh? The Men's Cheerleading Club?

00:15:50.980 --> 00:15:52.610
You mean that?

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:56.400
Wearing itty-bitty skirts and dancing
around waving pom-poms in the air?

00:15:56.400 --> 00:15:58.730
Don't tell me you're a bunch of pervs!

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:02.190
No! We cheer people on!

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:04.980
People putting their hearts
into whatever they do,

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:06.690
looking straight ahead!

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:09.860
It says so right on that flier!

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:13.610
Become a hero by
supporting someone else.

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:17.740
Gain the strength to inspire
someone to greater heights.

00:16:18.440 --> 00:16:20.900
Welp, we're done here,
so we'll be leaving...

00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:22.190
What the hell?!

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:25.820
So you infiltrated my club
just to poach my members!

00:16:35.980 --> 00:16:38.360
Nice double-leg takedown.

00:16:44.030 --> 00:16:46.030
So you did judo!

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:47.530
Well, yeah.

00:16:47.530 --> 00:16:49.980
You're pretty strong, Bandou.

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:51.320
Haru is fine.

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:53.230
Oh, and you can call me Kazu.

00:16:53.230 --> 00:16:54.860
Haru, Kazu...

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:57.030
Harukazuuu~!

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:59.860
That sounds like an entirely different name!

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:05.110
Those two will definitely contact us.

00:17:05.110 --> 00:17:07.780
How can you be so sure?

00:17:07.780 --> 00:17:09.440
Didn't you see his towel?

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:12.230
Covered in messages from old teammates.

00:17:12.230 --> 00:17:16.530
They're the kind of guys who
love doing things as a group.

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:21.570
Look who's talking.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.070
I can't!

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:34.440
I'm not quite there yet.

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:35.730
No, that was great!

00:17:35.730 --> 00:17:37.230
You've got what it takes, Ton!

00:17:37.230 --> 00:17:38.650
You did it!

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:42.650
You've been practicing a lot, haven't you?

00:17:42.650 --> 00:17:44.190
Just a little bit.

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:46.730
Whaddaya mean just a little?

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:49.940
By the way, have those two
contacted you yet?

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:52.400
No, not yet.

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:53.820
So it didn't work.

00:17:53.820 --> 00:17:55.400
That's too bad.

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:57.610
I wouldn't give up hope yet...

00:17:57.610 --> 00:17:58.860
Oh, that's right!

00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:00.690
I've been working hard on something, too!

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:03.680
Formation

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:03.680
Motions

00:18:02.690 --> 00:18:03.980
Kazu...

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:05.360
